    "claims": [
      {
        "claim": "When I see a number like 140 sick in Chinatown, I don't see a number — I see the families I work with every day. Most of them aren't going to the hospital. They're staying home because that's what we do. The daughter takes the bus from Fruitvale to cook. The nephew calls in late to pick up prescriptions. I'm the one who helps figure out who needs a home health aide, who needs their meds delivered, who just needs someone to check in. The hospital has six of our folks right now — the ones who really couldn't stay home. The rest of us are doing what we've always done: taking care of each other, block by block, door by door.",
        "sourceRef": "citizenVoice PRESS Marisio Curazo"
      }
